1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,879
What if time moved at a different speed

2
00:00:02,919 --> 00:00:03,837
in every room?

3
00:00:03,877 --> 00:00:06,506
In your house, the bedroom races ahead,

4
00:00:06,546 --> 00:00:08,764
the kitchen walks at normal pace,

5
00:00:08,804 --> 00:00:11,639
and the cellar crawls like a sleepy snail.

6
00:00:12,950 --> 00:00:15,417
You step into the fast bedroom and a

7
00:00:15,457 --> 00:00:16,461
day flashes by.

8
00:00:16,501 --> 00:00:18,620
The sun zips across the window,

9
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:20,361
plants shoot up and wilt,

10
00:00:20,401 --> 00:00:22,798
and your pillow fort builds itself,

11
00:00:22,838 --> 00:00:23,981
then falls apart.

12
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:28,876
In the kitchen, a single egg takes years to fry.

13
00:00:28,916 --> 00:00:31,472
A water drop hangs in the air like

14
00:00:31,512 --> 00:00:32,618
a tiny crystal.

15
00:00:32,658 --> 00:00:35,367
You wait for your toast so long that

16
00:00:35,407 --> 00:00:37,353
you start writing a novel.

17
00:00:38,650 --> 00:00:41,002
The hallway is the strangest place.

18
00:00:41,042 --> 00:00:43,531
Your left hand sits in the slow room,

19
00:00:43,571 --> 00:00:45,718
your right hand in the fast one,

20
00:00:45,758 --> 00:00:49,681
and you wave goodbye to yourself in two different decades.

21
00:00:50,950 --> 00:00:52,732
You soon learn the tricks.

22
00:00:52,772 --> 00:00:54,904
Do the dishes in the slow room,

23
00:00:54,944 --> 00:00:56,235
and no time passes.

24
00:00:56,275 --> 00:00:57,847
Study in the fast room,

25
00:00:57,887 --> 00:01:01,981
and you finish your homework before the pizza even arrives.

26
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:06,531
Physicists would say time can't really vary between

27
00:01:06,571 --> 00:01:09,396
rooms, so this is only a thought experiment.

28
00:01:09,436 --> 00:01:12,000
Still, it makes you wonder how much time

29
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:14,996
you're wasting in the fast rooms of your life.

30
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:17,369
Here is the twist.

31
00:01:17,409 --> 00:01:19,495
Grandpa sits in the slowest room,

32
00:01:19,535 --> 00:01:22,006
reading the same page of his newspaper.

33
00:01:22,046 --> 00:01:24,840
The family realises the cellar isn't broken.

34
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:27,996
It's where a quiet minute can last all afternoon.

35
00:01:29,250 --> 00:01:32,671
So the whole family gathers in the cellar for dinner.

36
00:01:32,711 --> 00:01:34,173
Candles barely flicker.

37
00:01:34,213 --> 00:01:35,806
Steam hangs like ribbons.

38
00:01:35,846 --> 00:01:37,569
One hour feels like a week,

39
00:01:37,609 --> 00:01:40,639
and you finally get to enjoy every single bite.
